[SIZE=2]Unmodified OPL starting a game from a virtual drive, through its own IOP reboot. That is the one stock PCSX2 cannot do.[/SIZE]


[SIZE=7][B]RIPPCSX2[/B][/SIZE]
[I]A PlayStation 2 emulator built for testing, made to be driven by you or by an AI agent.[/I]

[URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPCSX2/releases/latest/download/RIPPCSX2-windows-x64-avx2.zip'][B]Download for Windows[/B][/URL]  |  [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPCSX2/releases/latest/download/RIPPCSX2-linux-x64.AppImage'][B]Download for Linux[/B][/URL]  |  [URL='https://akilluminati47.github.io/RIPPCSX2/'][B]Website[/B][/URL]  |  [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPCSX2'][B]GitHub[/B][/URL]
[SIZE=2]One rolling release that is never stale. Bring your own BIOS dump. Unzip it anywhere: it keeps its settings in its own folder and leaves any PCSX2 you already have alone.[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[SIZE=3]RIPPCSX2 is PCSX2 v2.9.96 with what a PS2 homebrew developer needs to see the real thing. It began as the test lab for [URL='https://akilluminati47.github.io/RIPPS2/']RIPPS2[/URL], and it is for anyone building PS2 homebrew, themes, tools or game fixes. It is an unofficial fork, not affiliated with the PCSX2 team. Please report problems to the RIPPS2 project, never to PCSX2.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]It behaves like a PS2 where stock does not[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][LEFT][B]Stock OPL starts games.[/B] OPL reboots the IOP through a device it registers itself, named host. PCSX2 grabbed every host: open for itself, so OPL stopped at "file 'host0:' can't open". A program's own host device now gets its own opens.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]In-game menus over real frames.[/B] The EE's data write breakpoint works, in the interpreter and the recompiler, so OPL's GSM and RIPPS2's in-game menu can hook the GS registers as on a console.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]EXIT GAME reaches the browser.[/B] A SIO2 interrupt was being lost over an IOP reboot, which left OSDSYS waiting on the memory card with a black screen.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]True 720p and 1080i.[/B] Shown 16:9, captured at 1280 x 720 and 1920 x 1080, screenshots the same. Stock draws them 4:3, and moves 1080i up 42 lines.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPCSX2/rippcsx2/docs/release/exit-game-browser.jpg[/IMG]
[SIZE=2]EXIT GAME from RIPPS2's in-game menu, landing in the console's own browser[/SIZE]

