[SIZE=5][B]RIPART: art and decoys for themers[/B][/SIZE]
A new tool in the RIPPCSX2 menu, built on OPL Manager's art database: 16,313 games, read straight from danielb7390's backup on archive.org without downloading the whole 5.2 GB.
[LIST]
[*][LEFT][B]Decoys.[/B] Pick a drive, press one button: a dozen random full sets appear as game entries in OPL or RIPPS2 straight away, so you can judge a theme on a real list with no games on the drive. A decoy is a 2 KB entry for art only and does not start. One button takes them away again.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Every game on a checkbox list.[/B] Search it, tick what you want, and choose the art types. Pick a game to see each piece of its art: the full set is ticked to start, so untick what you don't want.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Find Games With No Art.[/B] It reads a drive's DVD, CD and POPS folders and ticks the games that have no cover.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]ART folder or art.tar.[/B] Write loose files for OPL and RIPPS2, or add to one art.tar for RIPPS2's ART Pack. It never replaces a file that is already there.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]
[SIZE=2]akilluminati47 helped bring OPL Manager its 8-bit PNG art and its 128 x 128 disc icons, so RIPART reads a database that already suits the PS2. Thanks to danielb7390 for OPL Manager and for keeping those backups public.[/SIZE]
